"en": "The Prophet ﷺ told of a man in open land who heard a voice in a cloud say, water the garden of so-and-so. The cloud moved aside and poured its water onto rocky ground, where one channel gathered all of it. He followed the water and found a man standing in his garden, turning the water with his spade. He asked his name, and it was the very name he had heard in the cloud. The gardener asked why he wanted to know. He told him about the voice, and asked what he did with his garden. The gardener said: since you ask, I look at what it produces; I give a third in charity, my family and I eat a third, and I put a third back into it.",
